call Includes/Normal
# Like Maze.con, but the walls come from the real WallPerceptor on the camera image (MZ-019). Only the AprilTags are
# faked from the ground truth pose until the real detector is evaluated in simulation.
# The maze comes from Config/Scenes/Includes/Maze/current.maze, written by maze_to_scene.py next to the scene.
for Cognition mr AprilTagPercept OracledMazePerceptsProvider
# Hide the game clock and score board: no game time or goals in the maze.
dr debugDrawing3d:representation:GameState off
call Includes/Views
# In this scene the walls render darker than the floor; the WallPerceptor accepts steps in either direction.
# Wall perceptor views: boundary pixels in the upper camera image (green boundary, red clear column), the points and
# the percept in the robot frame on the field view "wallPerceptor".
vid all module:WallPerceptor:boundary
vf wallPerceptor
vfd wallPerceptor module:WallPerceptor:points
vfd wallPerceptor representation:WallPercept:field
# No automatic referee: it would penalize the robot for standing in the opponent half.
ar off
gc playing
dr unmute on
